MatchedObjectDescriptor.QualificationSummary:
Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GG/GS-12 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector performing the following duties such as: 1. Working knowledge of Navy or DOD executive customer set and executive customer priorities and information needs; 2. Understanding of the Intelligence Community or Defense Intelligence Enterprise organization, roles, strategies and guidance, and federated analysis and production;
3. Demonstrated ability to directly engage, collaborate, and liaise with executive customers;
4. Developing processes and procedures to improve internal and external communications;
5. Developing solutions to cross-organizational issues and; 6. Advocating for support needed to fulfill customer mission requirements. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management website: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series http://archive.opm.gov/qualifications/Standards/IORs/gs0100/0132.htm

MajorDuties:
As a INTELLIGENCE SPECIALIST (CHIEF OF STAFF) you will be responsible for the following duties: - Reviewing, assigning and tracking tasks assigned from DCSA HQ, other agency directorates and DoD organizations using the Correspondence and Task Management System (CATMS);
- Coordinating with DCSA HQ and other internal organizations to ensure effective communications are maintained and CI interests are represented; - Developing, coordinating, and tracking internal and external staff actions to ensure timely, efficient actions are processed within established guidance and processes; - Working with senior staff members, action officers, managers, team leaders, and operating officials to ensure proper response to CI actions and to resolve or mitigate both short and long term issues;
- Leading initiatives within CI to ensure effective cross-agency integration for risk-based analysis and mitigation decisions.
